#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536875 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162096 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e91708c9-67e2-5228-84fd-1f4ea60064ac" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Mean-Deviation Form of an Observation Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e278261-12a2-522a-865f-2ee4f991690d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536414} {:answer/id #uuid "95c87fe0-b27d-523b-b97f-283a3892f373" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536522} {:answer/id #uuid "ad6e45b4-0d19-5a65-9da0-878c4f37d052" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536562} {:answer/id #uuid "c24f6fe3-8f3b-5e4f-87ee-cd603ef7bb00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536590} {:answer/id #uuid "c4625cbc-5b19-59bd-9eb5-2085cc809466" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536595}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad6e45b4-0d19-5a65-9da0-878c4f37d052" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536562} :answer-field/id #uuid "9980a067-163c-5305-b9d5-aeb44a51e2ee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536761}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b9e3535a-6a10-557b-a90a-dcbee5f059a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-138608" :question/problem "$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 7 & 5 & 9\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the observation matrix $X$ above, where the individual observations are given in columns. Find the mean-deviation form of $X.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the mean-deviation form of the observation matrix\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}| & | &  & | \\\\ {x}_{1} & {x}_{2} & ⋯ & {x}_{n} \\\\ | & | &  & |\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis given by \n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}| & | &  & | \\\\ {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} & ⋯ & {b}_{n} \\\\ | & | &  & |\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nwhere ${b}_{i}={x}_{i}-m$ for $i=1,2,…,n,$ and $m$ is sample mean vector.\n\nFrom the matrix, we have that  \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nAs a result, the sample mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{1}{3}({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}([\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 21\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} & ={x}_{1}-m=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {b}_{2} & ={x}_{2}-m=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {b}_{3} & ={x}_{3}-m=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,  the mean-deviation form is\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536842 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162096 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e91708c9-67e2-5228-84fd-1f4ea60064ac" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Mean-Deviation Form of an Observation Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "57509c8b-6b98-51aa-9762-9963caf04358" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536435} {:answer/id #uuid "581f54a2-60c9-5dc5-bb4d-f8f318fe2d6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536440} {:answer/id #uuid "7a4429f4-c191-50e8-be52-084fe635f47b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536488} {:answer/id #uuid "bfecac8a-fa87-5d62-a946-7f122c1e66c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536585} {:answer/id #uuid "f1218c8e-974e-52d6-b624-68fd43f78159" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536667}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bfecac8a-fa87-5d62-a946-7f122c1e66c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536585} :answer-field/id #uuid "b518b34a-8d6e-54eb-93d9-d3cb5a0505b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536774}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6a4bb009-1382-5d80-b122-5cf6749f1552" :question/math-academy-id "q-138615" :question/problem "$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 7 & 5 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the observation matrix $X$ above, where the individual observations are given in columns. Find the mean-deviation form of $X.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the mean-deviation form of the observation matrix\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}| & | &  & | \\\\ {x}_{1} & {x}_{2} & ⋯ & {x}_{n} \\\\ | & | &  & |\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis given by \n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}| & | &  & | \\\\ {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} & ⋯ & {b}_{n} \\\\ | & | &  & |\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nwhere ${b}_{i}={x}_{i}-m$ for $i=1,2,…,n,$ and $m$ is sample mean vector.\n\nFrom the matrix, we have that  \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nAs a result, the sample mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{1}{3}({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}([\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} & ={x}_{1}-m=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {b}_{2} & ={x}_{2}-m=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {b}_{3} & ={x}_{3}-m=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,  the mean-deviation form is\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536835 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162095 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dc84d72a-b9f3-5f99-aa23-31cfe6910d49" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Covariance Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c32cbe8-c57b-5bf3-a19d-03d660a7ac0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}34 & -17 \\\\ -17 & -29\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536351} {:answer/id #uuid "4ba53bf9-6d2f-55fc-bcb0-4c3a502a927e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}34 & 7 \\\\ 7 & -29\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536406} {:answer/id #uuid "99ee16dd-f5ce-5d55-9f57-ac836de565b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}12 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -27\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536530} {:answer/id #uuid "a35b201c-f9c8-5ef5-99f4-35d4c0535194" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}46 & 77 \\\\ 77 & 21\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536547} {:answer/id #uuid "f3949942-a93b-5278-9bdf-682422d7e809" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}10 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 42\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536674}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f3949942-a93b-5278-9bdf-682422d7e809" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}10 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 42\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536674} :answer-field/id #uuid "fef71c07-ba83-5d64-938a-f5aa72763b99" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536804}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5926666e-0db3-5dee-9762-40fbc13f71e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-138627" :question/problem "$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -1 & -4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the observation matrix $B$ in the mean-deviation form above, where the individual observations are given in columns. \nFind the sample covariance matrix of the data." :question/worked-solution "Recall that  the sample covariance matrix is given by\n\n$$\nC=\\frac{1}{n-1}B{B}^{T},\n$$\n\nwhere $B$ is the observation matrix in the mean-deviation form, and $n$ is the number of observations.\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =\\frac{1}{4-1}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -1 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}10 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 42\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536822 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162095 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dc84d72a-b9f3-5f99-aa23-31cfe6910d49" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Covariance Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "313c180d-6683-5895-8319-1cc5e1d0047d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}62 & -69 \\\\ -69 & 242\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536360} {:answer/id #uuid "3528ecab-4caa-5dc2-8341-f72254cce85e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}25 & -25 \\\\ -25 & 47\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536366} {:answer/id #uuid "4c4801ac-f3c0-54c9-9d9b-068066aba1b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}52 & 30 \\\\ 30 & 250\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536409} {:answer/id #uuid "551ede1c-3223-5e2a-a363-e21869ad5829" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}65 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 340\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536431} {:answer/id #uuid "ff8daa35-c661-577d-b35d-32e5b20ab32b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}30 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 69\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536692}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "313c180d-6683-5895-8319-1cc5e1d0047d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}62 & -69 \\\\ -69 & 242\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536360} :answer-field/id #uuid "677e14b0-94a5-52de-a477-ccd697d060de" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536749}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2f2cb4c0-5e13-5762-90d1-d095feb4a65e" :question/math-academy-id "q-138631" :question/problem "$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 & -6 & 1 \\\\ 10 & -6 & 5 & -9\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the observation matrix $B$ in the mean-deviation form above, where the individual observations are given in columns. \nFind the sample covariance matrix of the data." :question/worked-solution "Recall that  the sample covariance matrix is given by\n\n$$\nC=\\frac{1}{n-1}B{B}^{T},\n$$\n\nwhere $B$ is the observation matrix in the mean-deviation form, and $n$ is the number of observations.\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =\\frac{1}{4-1}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 & -6 & 1 \\\\ 10 & -6 & 5 & -9\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 10 \\\\ 5 & -6 \\\\ -6 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -9\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}62 & -69 \\\\ -69 & 242\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536884 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162095 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dc84d72a-b9f3-5f99-aa23-31cfe6910d49" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Covariance Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f060f18-5f38-57d0-8035-ee521e1efa10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 42\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536447} {:answer/id #uuid "63f36174-881c-57cb-888e-5b635ad28017" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -10\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536456} {:answer/id #uuid "6a9c88b3-2c09-54a3-99c5-91c575160cb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 42\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536463} {:answer/id #uuid "82ed669f-a9bd-5e1c-8760-9d608342f7c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 42\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536499} {:answer/id #uuid "e3398816-b77b-5ead-950a-9a70459413a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -10\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536639}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f060f18-5f38-57d0-8035-ee521e1efa10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 42\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536447} :answer-field/id #uuid "63610fdd-4a0f-5e58-8e91-40c9b79c1b2f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536744}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d39bfe0e-e6e3-509a-9ccb-2651e206d7a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-138639" :question/problem "$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 6 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the observation matrix $X$ above, where the individual observations are given in columns. Find the sample covariance matrix of the data." :question/worked-solution "Recall that  the sample covariance matrix is given by\n\n$$\nC=\\frac{1}{n-1}B{B}^{T},\n$$\n\nwhere $B$ is the observation matrix in the mean-deviation form, and $n$ is the number of observations.\n\nSo, we first need to compute the mean-deviation form of our observation matrix.\n\nThe sample mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{1}{3}({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}([\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} & ={x}_{1}-m=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {b}_{2} & ={x}_{2}-m=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {b}_{3} & ={x}_{3}-m=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,  the mean-deviation form is\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & -1 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, the sample covariance matrix is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =\\frac{1}{3-1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & -1 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 42\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
